module lib/hf/rohf
  Restricted open-shell Hartree-Fock (ROHF), checked against PySCF 2.5.0.

  ROHF has one set of orbitals shared by both spins, split three ways. Closed
  orbitals hold an alpha and a beta electron, open orbitals hold one alpha
  electron each, and the virtual orbitals are empty. Unlike UHF, the result
  is a state of definite total spin.

  No single Fock matrix has these orbitals as its eigenvectors, so the loop
  (lib/hf/scf_loop) diagonalizes an effective Fock matrix built by a coupling
  (lib/hf/coupling). The coupling changes the path of the iteration but not
  where it ends. This module holds the ROHF checks: PySCF's energies with
  every coupling, `E_UHF <= E_ROHF`, the fixed-point step on O2's two
  states, and which accelerators reach each SCF regime.

rohf_t_import  @67f58048
  how   From one O2 6-31G pair of spin densities: take the plain step and
        compare; converge further with tighter tolerances; step again. The
        measurements come back as lib/hf/rhf's `RhfImport` record.

rohf_t_regime  @e320b034
  what  Test helper: how far one run lands from its reference energy, for a
        method, a closed or open shell and an accelerator.

  system         water STO-3G for a closed shell, OH STO-3G for an open one, with its reference energy
  run            run the SCF from the core guess
  return the energy gap
